  "details": "While the total number of players can be useful for identifying popular or high quality worlds, it often isn't very useful for finding people to spontaneously play with. Finding a world with players and discovering that none of the instances is joinable makes browsing through the worlds daunting. \n\n  \n\nHaving the number of people in accessible instances visible without having to open the details of each world one by one would greatly help the discoverability of these worlds and instances. This information should be displayed along the total number of players, or at least be available at a glance.   \n\n  \n\nAs a bonus:  \n\n- Have a separate ranking of worlds based on this metric\n\n- Allow showing only worlds that have at least one reachable player",
